            <ArticleTitle>Profile of reslizumab in eosinophilic disease and its potential in the treatment of poorly controlled eosinophilic asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2147/BTT.S30133</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Eosinophils are important proinflammatory cells that make a major contribution to the inflammation seen in allergic diseases including asthma. Interleukin-5 is central to eosinophil maturation, release from the bone marrow, and subsequent accumulation, activation, and persistence in the tissues. Reslizumab (Cinquil™) is a humanized monoclonal antibody with potent interleukin-5 neutralizing effects, which represents a potential treatment for poorly controlled eosinophilic asthma. This review will consider the current status of the clinical development of reslizumab for asthma and in other inflammatory diseases with a marked eosinophilic component.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
